<!--Post: 3928--><!--Time: 1105418268-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3928"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Skov<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Skov<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 10, 2005 - 8:37 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I dont belive that what the WPD released about BTK has to have any truth in it whatsoever, BTK could very well have  given info just to through off the police compleatly. <BR> <BR>I have TONS of real info on this guy I have researched him the whole day, but can not post it here on the forum without shouting his name out loud and I also have his picture wich match the BTK sketch very well. <BR> <BR>This man is 55 wich means he would have been 23 at the Otero murder, that would work IMO. He was a full time maneger for a quite big bussiness at 19 years old! <BR> <BR>concerning his identity,I have NOT mentioned his name and if you read through this forum, a LOT of people are mentioned by name wich I did not. <BR> <BR>IMO this man is actually exactly the kind of person that I always though BTK would turn out to bee. Just my opinion, not saying that he is BTK AT ALL, just saying he fits MY humble amature profile. <BR> <BR>Here is the sketch of BTK <BR><a href="http://www.crimelibrary.com/serial_killers/unsolved/btk/collide_4.html?sect=4" target=_top>http://www.crimelibrary.com/serial_killers/unsolve d/btk/collide_4.html?sect=4</a> <BR> <BR>And here is the person I think look likethe sketch, NO name. <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.google.dk/search?q=cache:wKQHHwNCXtgJ:www.f5wichita.com/news/index.php%3Fpubdate%3D2003-03-20%26story%3D260%2B%2B%22Darryl%2BSmith%22%2B%2Bwichita%2B%2Bwarren&amp;hl=en" target=_top>http://www.google.dk/search?q=cache:wKQHHwNCXtgJ:w ww.f5wichita.com/news/index.php%3Fpubdate%3D2003-0 3-20%26story%3D260&#43;&#43;%22Darryl&#43;Smith%22&#43;%2Bwichita&#43; %2Bwarren&amp;hl=en</a> <BR> <BR>copy this two pics and put them beside each other and let me know what you think <BR> <BR>Would you please deleet the last photlink Tom? there is no function so that I can edit myself, just wanted Chifron to see the resemblance <BR> <BR>skov <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3928-->
<!--Post: 3938--><!--Time: 1105426111-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3938"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Pax56<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Pax56<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 10, 2005 - 10:48 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Skov - your posts always make me smile - whether I agree or not.  If the pictures tell a story, I would say the poor man is innocent, too, and deserves a bit of an apology from us.  However, that BTK picture does resemble at least one existing suspect known to WPD - certainly more than this guy. <BR> <BR>Ciao!  -pax<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3938-->
<!--Post: 3964--><!--Time: 1105472364-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3964"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Chiefron<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Chiefron<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, January 11, 2005 - 11:39 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Skov, <BR> <BR>I have compared photos of your suspect with the sketch and find no reason to think that if the sketch is that of BTK, that your suspect is the same person. The sketch shows a young male, probably of hispanic origin, with features and skin tone consistent with indigenous mexican indian populations or mixed african hispanic populations from the carribean islands and rim rather than euro-descended hispanic populations. Your suspect looks very anglo with high cheek bones and narrow dark eyes hinting at possible north american indian mixing. The black and white photo leaves lots of room for skin tone interpretation, but he does not look to have much in the way of dark skin. Perhaps a slight olive complexion or simply a tan. <BR> <BR>Your suspect&#39;s list of employment consists of a variety of jobs that would keep him in doors most of his day. Not jobs that would lend themselves to sun darkening of ones skin such are construction or farm labor. <BR> <BR>However, even if I could see a resemblance, which I cannot, I would have severe problems considering this man a suspect. Primarily because he is so far off from the profile of BTK. <BR> <BR>As I said, your suspect is both 10 years younger than BTK proclaims to be, an age that fits with the profile of both BTK and the vast majority of serial killers. <BR> <BR>Your suspects personal history as I know it also does not jive with either BTKs admissions or with any profile ever created of him or any other serial killer. <BR> <BR>Your suspect is a brash, arrogant, outspoken member of his community. These are things that have helped to make him a successful business man. They do not, however, point toward any propensity to sociopathy. In fact they point away from it. How many times have you heard it said about a serial killer by those that knew him, that he was a nice, quiet person who they would never suspect? Just about every instance that I know of. There is a good reason for this. Your suspect just does not fit in that category.  <BR> <BR>Your suspect is a respected, successful business man. Aside from Bundy I have a hard time thinking of any known serial killer that fit that mold and even in the Bundy case, his potential for success was never met, but rather supplanted by his need to kill. <BR> <BR>This is in no way a personal attack against you Skov. I am simply arguing against your profile in what I hope is a logical manner. This is what I do to suspects and cases provided to me when I am assigned as IO. You built up a case for your profile with evidence you think makes it strong. I am simply arguing those peices. Now you can attack my points or provide evidence that you think refutes them. After we do this a while and we have sorted the grains from the chaff we will hopefully be left with only those things that we can call absolute truths. <BR> <BR>Profiles rely on suppositions to develop suspects. However once you start looking at the suspect to build a case you must rely on provable facts to relate them to the crime. Unfortunately I would never have considered this man a suspect because no supposition about BTK matches the reality of this man.  <BR> <BR>A couple points that you make that do fit the profile, such as having recently lost a family member, had a recent public humiliation etc to respark his killing, ignore the fact that this suspects known history is 180 degrees out from that of the typical serial killer. BTK may certainly be a different breed of killer than any we have ever seen, but history tells he probably is not. <BR> <BR>I like the idea of debating this suspects merits in this thread. However it is pretty simple for anyone to infer who we are discussing so I think it best to discuss it via e-mail <BR> <BR> <a href="mailto:hkenley@san.rr.com">hkenley@san.rr.com</a>  <BR> <BR>Drop me a line with your research notes and I will reply with my rebuttals and my notes on your suspect as well.  <BR> <BR>Keep in mind, even though I do not think this suspect is BTK, I am more than willing to continue the discussion and let you try to convince me otherwise. <BR> <BR>Keep digging and I will do the same. Thats what its all about.  <BR> <BR>Ron <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
